menu "Shelly Wi-Fi maintenance mode"

    config SHELLY_MAINTENANCE
        bool "Wi-Fi maintenance mode (hold the button 5 s)"
        default y
        help
            Holding the button 5 s restarts the device into a boot of its own
            with Matter and Thread off: it runs an open Wi-Fi network and a
            web page at 192.168.33.1 that installs a firmware update (the
            Matter .ota file). See docs/BUTTON-AND-LED.md and docs/UPDATING.md.
            Without it, the 5 s hold is refused.

    config SHELLY_MAINTENANCE_IDLE_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Return to normal after this long with the page closed (s)"
        depends on SHELLY_MAINTENANCE
        default 600
        range 60 3600

    config SHELLY_FACTORY_DUMP
        bool "Download Shelly's stock data partitions from the page (read only)"
        depends on SHELLY_MAINTENANCE
        default n
        help
            Adds GET /part?name=... to the Wi-Fi mode page: a read-only copy of
            one of the stock regions this firmware never uses (shelly, fs_0,
            fs_1, zb_storage), to study what Shelly stores there, such as
            factory calibration. Never this firmware's own nvs. The shelly
            partition may hold the device's own keys and the Wi-Fi mode
            network is open, so this is for boards being brought up only.

endmenu
